# Test: interface backend vpp accepts flow-export counter export without sampling or conntrack.
# Question: does `ze config validate` accept `flow-export` under `interface
#           backend vpp` when `sampling` is absent and `conntrack enabled` is
#           absent/false?
#           A unit test cannot prove both `flow-export` predicates leave plain
#           counter export accepted in `ze config validate`.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-5 survivor -- counter-only
#            flow export declares no kernel-only forwarding requirement and
#            validates under VPP.
# PREVENTS: refusing the whole `flow-export` root under VPP instead of only
#           its kernel-only `sampling` and `conntrack` subtrees.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
	backend vpp;
}
flow-export {
	collector sflow1 {
		address 10.0.0.50;
		port 6343;
		protocol sflow;
		agent-address 127.0.0.1;
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid
